From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a page that gets no begin frames says why

In the CI VM repro a window froze with its compositor getting no begin
frames at all ("begin frames 0, last 10 s ago") while its main thread
waited on a commit it had asked for. Nothing said whether the page
stopped asking for begin frames or viz stopped sending them, so this
logs both sides at once:

- The compositor-thread line (0248) adds the scheduler: whether it has
  and watches a begin frame source, whether it wants begin frames, and
  the state machine flags that decide that (visible, source paused,
  frame sink state, begin main frame state, pending tree, redraw,
  prepare tiles, frames awaiting ack). It also says why it cannot draw
  and the viewport size.
- viz logs, once per starvation, a frame sink whose client has wanted
  begin frames for 3 s and got none: whether it has a begin frame
  source and whether that is paused, whether it observes it, how many
  begin frames the source offered since the last one sent and the last
  reason it held one back, how far its unanswered begin frames are
  from the throttle and stop limits, and when it last sent one.

Log only, and the viz check is a 3 s timer only while a client wants
begin frames and gets none.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on crux.
